\title{Decoder-only Transformer architecture}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{notes}

\p{The continuation law in \ref{ftip-000I} specifies what probabilities a
language model exposes. A decoder-only Transformer specifies how a sequence of
token identifiers is transformed into those probabilities. This section
introduces one component at a time, with dimensions fixed before the component
formulas are used.}

